This directory is the default repository location for deployable apps in a deployment server 
configuration.

For details on configuring as a deployment server, see 
$SPLUNK_HOME/etc/system/README/serverclass.conf.spec, serverclass.conf.example or the Admin manual 
at http://docs.splunk.com/Documentation.

# Custom Naming conventions for this lab
## Infrastructure apps: <scope>_<function>
- The scope dictates which tier  the app is for: all, idx, hf, uf or sh
- all means any splunk instance that needs it. serverclass.conf will decide which host actually gets it.
- Examples: all_indexes -> Defines indexes for all indexers, uf_outputs_to_hf -> defines outputs for ufs to hfs

## Data apps: <source>_<function>
- Source is the data source name, like flog or pythonLogGen
- The function represents what the app does for the source
- Examples: flog_props_search -> Defines the search time props for flog, flog_inputs -> Defines the inputs for flog i.e. the monitor stanza

# Usage of prefixes:
Prefixes should be added to the app name when required to enforce precedence.
